From 7de72c5b43c86dc7e751dcb3a71aaa5496b40f6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:00:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 158/177] ASoC: meson: aiu: put the channel status bytes in the
 right order

The SPDIF encoder takes the channel status word as two 16 bit halves,
each holding the bits in the order they go on the wire: the datasheet
says AIU_958_chstat_l0 "contains Bits 15:0 of the channel status word.
Note that bit zero of the channel status word is sent out first", so
byte 0 belongs in the low half of the register and byte 1 in the high
half.

The driver writes them the other way round, and has since it was added,
so every subframe carries byte 1 where the receiver looks for byte 0 and
byte 3 where it looks for byte 2.  A receiver is therefore told the
category code in place of the mode bits and, worse, reads the sample
rate out of byte 2 rather than byte 3: a stream is announced as 44.1kHz
whatever it is, because byte 2 is zero and zero is 44.1kHz.

The vendor driver writes 0x8206 and 0x0900 where this one writes 0x0682
and 0x0009, for the same stream on the same silicon.

It is hard to notice for linear PCM, where the receiver locks to the
rate it is given and the channel status is advisory.  It is not hard to
notice for a compressed stream at a high frame rate, where a receiver
told 44.1kHz while the frame runs at 768kHz loses lock every few
seconds.

The AXG encoder already gets this right.

Fixes: 6ae9ca9ce986 ("ASoC: meson: aiu: add i2s and spdif support")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/meson/aiu-encoder-spdif.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/meson/aiu-encoder-spdif.c b/sound/soc/meson/aiu-encoder-spdif.c
index 97da60db2c4d..5d654e17c45f 100644
--- a/sound/soc/meson/aiu-encoder-spdif.c
+++ b/sound/soc/meson/aiu-encoder-spdif.c
@@ -80,12 +80,12 @@ static int aiu_encoder_spdif_setup_cs_word(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 		return ret;
 
 	/* Write the 1st half word */
-	val = cs[1] | cs[0] << 8;
+	val = cs[0] | cs[1] << 8;
 	snd_soc_component_write(component, AIU_958_CHSTAT_L0, val);
 	snd_soc_component_write(component, AIU_958_CHSTAT_R0, val);
 
 	/* Write the 2nd half word */
-	val = cs[3] | cs[2] << 8;
+	val = cs[2] | cs[3] << 8;
 	snd_soc_component_write(component, AIU_958_CHSTAT_L1, val);
 	snd_soc_component_write(component, AIU_958_CHSTAT_R1, val);
 
